{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1485845-ideas-for-familiar-characters","id":1485845,"title":"Ideas for familiar characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-05T09:33:38-07:00","id":1485845,"title":"Ideas for familiar characters","content":"So, I thought about making a thread about ideas for familiar characters, for both PCs and NPCs in general. I think I've never seen a thread on the subject.<br /> What are your ideas of interesting familiars for a mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T11:02:46-07:00","id":1485848,"title":"","content":"Not strictly a Mage character, but my Ananasi player got herself a Net Spider familiar who nests in her fetish phone and basically acts as its smart agent. We don't have a hacker or technomancer type in the group, so having a Weaver spirit who can jump in for that is useful- something that may also apply to a more Spirit oriented Tradition Mage who doesn't want to ignore newfangled things like &quot;The Internet&quot; completely. With the right Charms, you get an efficient way to do basic information searches or hacks while the players can continue with the plot.<br /> <br /> Aside from the utility, the more interesting part for me was playing the adaption period of the two very different mindsets when the familiar link between them kicked in. Net Spiders aren't known for their individuality or independence, and the poor thing was very confused for the first weeks when suddenly confronted with thoughts like 'what do I want?'. Same for the player who had to deal with really linear algorithmic thoughts (and echoes of the OneSong).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T16:09:56-07:00","id":1485862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1485845-ideas-for-familiar-characters?p=1485848#post1485848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not strictly a Mage character, but my Ananasi player got herself a Net Spider familiar who nests in her fetish phone and basically acts as its smart agent. We don't have a hacker or technomancer type in the group, so having a Weaver spirit who can jump in for that is useful- something that may also apply to a more Spirit oriented Tradition Mage who doesn't want to ignore newfangled things like &quot;The Internet&quot; completely. With the right Charms, you get an efficient way to do basic information searches or hacks while the players can continue with the plot.<br /> <br /> Aside from the utility, the more interesting part for me was playing the adaption period of the two very different mindsets when the familiar link between them kicked in. Net Spiders aren't known for their individuality or independence, and the poor thing was very confused for the first weeks when suddenly confronted with thoughts like 'what do I want?'. Same for the player who had to deal with really linear algorithmic thoughts (and echoes of the OneSong).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh! That's quite interesting! I've never heard of anything similar, and I've seen many different familiars, like cats (the one my players seem to always prefer lol), griffons, spiritual dogs, wolves, imps, even manticores and dragons lol, but it's the first time I hear about a Net Spider. That's quite creative and interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T04:04:34-07:00","id":1485975,"title":"","content":"I guess spirits are a more natural choice for Fera, while a Mage would probably prefer animals or Bygones. As you said, cats are the classic choice. I don't have Gods &amp; Monsters, so I don't know how ephemeral Familiars are handled there, but spirits are really diverse and there are plenty of interesting candidates for Familiars.<br /> <br /> For Euthanatoi or Nephandi, a Plasmic could make an interesting Familiar (basically as Wraith-ly Bygone). The story how they found each other is probably worth exploring through play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T08:48:06-07:00","id":1486423,"title":"","content":"I always like my outer space little green man alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T06:00:42-07:00","id":1486762,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on antagonist Familiars:<br /> <br /> <b>Nephandi:</b><br /> I think it's safe to say that no Familiar would survive the Caul if they go in together with a Nephandus-hopeful. They don't have an Avatar to invert, and in the worst case scenario, the additional consciousness could disturb the process or result in a <i>The Fly</i> scenario. If the Familiar does not enter, their link to the Mage would probably be severed after the process completes, since the emerging Nephandus is quite different from the person who went in.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping a Nephandus from acquiring a Familiar as Barabbus though, or Widderslainte from the get-go. They would probably tend towards Fomori, lesser Malfeans, or similar nightmares (Nightmare Chimeras?).<br /> <br /> <b>Marauders:</b><br /> The more interesting case. As far as I'm aware, there are no hard and fast rules how familiars react towards Quiet. Given the tight bond between Familiar and Mage, I would say Familiars represent one of the better options to pull a Mage back out. However, the same close link could mean the Familiar goes mad together with the Mage. And once the Mage goes over the edge, some weird things happen.<br /> <br /> One of the main benefits of a Familiar is the ability to act as a Paradox-fetch. Marauders, due to their nature, divert Paradox and hardly catch any themselves. That gives two options: either the Familiar catches <i>all </i>the diverted Paradox, in which case they go poof very quickly. Or the Familiar becomes part of the Marauder's personal reality bubble, and only fetches whatever gets through. A nice NPC hook could be a particularly strong-willed Familiar who controls the Marauder through manipulation, effectively becoming the main antagonist while the Marauder is a mere proxy.<br /> <br /> I don't see many 'complete' Marauders getting Familiars after the fact. After all, Familiars are sentient enough to realize their potential Mage partner has serious problems. As an inversion of the above scenario though, a PC playing a Familiar who has to babysit a Marauder NPC could be... fun?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T15:43:24-07:00","id":1486802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1485845-ideas-for-familiar-characters?p=1486762#post1486762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts on antagonist Familiars:<br /> <br /> <b>Nephandi:</b><br /> I think it's safe to say that no Familiar would survive the Caul if they go in together with a Nephandus-hopeful. They don't have an Avatar to invert, and in the worst case scenario, the additional consciousness could disturb the process or result in a <i>The Fly</i> scenario. If the Familiar does not enter, their link to the Mage would probably be severed after the process completes, since the emerging Nephandus is quite different from the person who went in.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping a Nephandus from acquiring a Familiar as Barabbus though, or Widderslainte from the get-go. They would probably tend towards Fomori, lesser Malfeans, or similar nightmares (Nightmare Chimeras?).<br /> <br /> <b>Marauders:</b><br /> The more interesting case. As far as I'm aware, there are no hard and fast rules how familiars react towards Quiet. Given the tight bond between Familiar and Mage, I would say Familiars represent one of the better options to pull a Mage back out. However, the same close link could mean the Familiar goes mad together with the Mage. And once the Mage goes over the edge, some weird things happen.<br /> <br /> One of the main benefits of a Familiar is the ability to act as a Paradox-fetch. Marauders, due to their nature, divert Paradox and hardly catch any themselves. That gives two options: either the Familiar catches <i>all </i>the diverted Paradox, in which case they go poof very quickly. Or the Familiar becomes part of the Marauder's personal reality bubble, and only fetches whatever gets through. A nice NPC hook could be a particularly strong-willed Familiar who controls the Marauder through manipulation, effectively becoming the main antagonist while the Marauder is a mere proxy.<br /> <br /> I don't see many 'complete' Marauders getting Familiars after the fact. After all, Familiars are sentient enough to realize their potential Mage partner has serious problems. As an inversion of the above scenario though, a PC playing a Familiar who has to babysit a Marauder NPC could be... fun?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very interesting thoughts, I never stopped to think about this issue with Nephandi's Familiars. One thing I need to add though is that I didn't enjoy God's &amp; Monsters as much as I thought I would. One thing I didn't get in the book is the lack of anything interesting about Dragons, it's like they were completely ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T05:38:30-07:00","id":1487569,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why the Nephandi Mages could not have a default and fairly normal selection of usual Familiars that the Verbenae and the Hermetics get. Especially considering that many Nephandi are former members of these Traditions or at least know a Nephandus who is. (or they know a current member of these Traditions !) Not every aspect / element in regard to the Nephandi has to be in the darker shades <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T10:23:16-07:00","id":1487617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to correct my assumptions on that one. <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i> actually has a short paragraph that mentions most Nephandi Familiars tend to have bonded with them before their fall, and presumably the bond survives them going through the Caul. It does also mention Fomori as a rare option, though.<br /> <br /> The same section also mentions Marauders picking up Bygones or warping their familiars into something fantastical after turning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:08:45-07:00","id":1487868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1485845-ideas-for-familiar-characters?p=1485848#post1485848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not strictly a Mage character, but my Ananasi player got herself a Net Spider familiar who nests in her fetish phone and basically acts as its smart agent. We don't have a hacker or technomancer type in the group, so having a Weaver spirit who can jump in for that is useful- something that may also apply to a more Spirit oriented Tradition Mage who doesn't want to ignore newfangled things like &quot;The Internet&quot; completely. With the right Charms, you get an efficient way to do basic information searches or hacks while the players can continue with the plot.<br /> <br /> Aside from the utility, the more interesting part for me was playing the adaption period of the two very different mindsets when the familiar link between them kicked in. Net Spiders aren't known for their individuality or independence, and the poor thing was very confused for the first weeks when suddenly confronted with thoughts like 'what do I want?'. Same for the player who had to deal with really linear algorithmic thoughts (and echoes of the OneSong).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh we had something similar but with the spider bound to an old WW2 field radio.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T05:27:08-07:00","id":1487874,"title":"","content":"- Chimerical Fae make for some good variations, and interesting for crossovers.<br /> <br /> - I used Techno controlled Xenomorphs in many games. I just love these monsters.<br /> <br /> - I never brought this one up in a game because Im always the ST and not a player, but one thing I've always wanted to see was a &quot;spirit of vampirism&quot;. And by that, I dont just mean some astral idea of it, I mean a spirit that embodies what cainites are. This could be placed in a regular animal. In fact, if anybody have ideas on this it would be great. Would this creature act as a <i>real</i> vampire? Could it learn disciplines, eat tass as blood only and be allergic to the Sun?<br /> Or, would it just be a ravenous uncontrollable Beast?<br /> What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}